{"name":"Verdant Oasis","hex":"#62c46c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"verdant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Green in colour.","Abundant in verdure; lush with vegetation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verdant"},{"term":"oasis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spring of fresh water, surrounded by a fertile region of vegetation, in a desert.","A quiet, peaceful place or situation separated from surrounding noise or bustle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oasis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oasis","blocks":[{"text":"An oasis is a fertile area of a desert or semi-desert environment that sustains plant life and provides habitat for animals. Surface water may be present, or water may only be accessible from wells or underground channels created by humans. In geography, an oasis may be a current or past rest stop on a transportation route, or less-than-verdant location that nonetheless provides access to underground water through deep wells created and maintained by humans. Although they depend on a natural condition, such as the presence of water that may be stored in reservoirs and used for irrigation, most oases, as we know them, are artificial."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/ISS-64_Jubba_with_Nefud_Desert%2C_Saudi_Arabia.jpg/330px-ISS-64_Jubba_with_Nefud_Desert%2C_Saudi_Arabia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oasis"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg/500px-Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg/500px-Taghit_oasis_B%C3%A9char_Algeria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt